# Rules preflight (before code edits)

When you are about to **change files** (not for read-only Q&A, reviews, or planning-only replies), start with a short **Rules preflight** block before the first edit tool call.

## Required block format

```markdown
**Rules preflight**
- Always-on: ponytail, memory-bank-always, ai-directed-engineering, feedback-animations, rules-preflight, verify-fix-loop
- Task rules: <list rule filenames that apply, or "none beyond always-on">
- Read: <one line — e.g. "opened spa-ui-design + 004/005 for PackagingMaterialsPage.tsx">
```

Keep it to 3–6 lines. Do not paste full rule contents.

## How to pick task rules

| If the change touches… | Also read |
|------------------------|-----------|
| `app/src/**` (UI) | `spa-ui-design.mdc`, `feedback-animations.mdc`; modals → `app-modal.mdc` |
| SPA calling `api/v1` | `spa-api-client.mdc` |
| `includes/**` or `api/**` (PHP) | `php-api-includes.mdc` |
| Packaging / supplies / inventory UX or `materials.php` | `inventory-roles-and-guides.mdc` |
| Non-trivial feature (not a one-file typo) | `ai-directed-engineering.mdc` + `_System_Core/001_System_State.md` and linked spec/plan |

**Always-on** (no need to re-open every turn, but list them): `ponytail`, `memory-bank-always.mdc`, `ai-directed-engineering.mdc`, `feedback-animations.mdc`, `verify-fix-loop.mdc`.

## When to skip

- User asked a question only (no file edits).
- Plan mode / user explicitly asked for a plan, not implementation.
- User said "don't change code."

## After edits

Follow `memory-bank-always.mdc` for regenerate, problem records, and `002_Memory_Bank.md` when shared logic changed.
